WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.690
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.690
<b>Episode 4
"Muromi-san and the Food Chain"</b>

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.240
File!

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.740
I think this is a threadsail filefish.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.330
This is a black scraper filefish.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.910
They've got a longer face than the threadsail,

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.590
so people called them "horse-faces," 
and that became their nickname.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.050
Isn't that mean?

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.420
Hiichan out!

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.000
What are you looking for?

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.160
What are you looking for? 
How to get rid of you.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.250
It's nice in the fall.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.040
There's plenty of different types 
of fish you can catch, too.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.040
<b>Sea Bream   Goby        Mahi-mahi      Round Greeneyes</b>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.040
<b>Broadbanded Thornyhead              Threadsail Filefish</b>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.040
<b>Golden Threadfin Bream       Atlantic Mackerel</b>

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.160
You can catch lots of fish 
during Japan's autumn?

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.520
It's not just limited to fish.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.270
There's also fruits and...

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.440
<i>What is this wild beast pressure I feel?!</i>

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.290
<i>That's a weird outfit she's wearing.</i>

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.880
Do you live around here?

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.610
Are your mom and dad not with you today?

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.720
My parents are the Himalayas.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.220
If I had to be specific, I would 
say the earth is my mother.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.790
Being mysterious for the sake of it?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.440
Muromi-san told me to wait here.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.930
What was that?!

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.340
She said there's a boy here who likes fishing,

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.870
so kill some time with him if you're bored.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.240
Sorry, Yetchi. Did you wait long?

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.670
Take a look at these persimmons.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.730
They have a sweet-salty taste 
from being in the sea—

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:56.450
File!

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.090
Oh no!

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.240
I told you not to use me as your meeting spot!

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.830
Don't bully Muromi-san.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.830
Hey, you black scraper!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.160
I wasn't really bullying her.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.620
That's right.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.290
In a comedy duo,

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.000
we'd be the straight man and funny man.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.310
We fit together perfectly, 
like a man and woman would—

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.440
What are you going on about?

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.410
<b>Oh really...</b>

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.580
So who is this girl, Muromi-san?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.550
Yeti.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:26.990
Yeti?!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.090
She's tiny! No one's gonna find her...

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.790
She said she's never been to Japan.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:37.070
And fall's the best time to come, 
and the food's the best then, too.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.390
So I was thinking of showing her 
places with pretty fall foliage.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.920
You sure know a lot of 
legendary creatures, Muromi-san.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.300
Stop it.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.120
So Yeti, how did you come to Japan, anyway?

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.090
You can't get a passport, right?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.930
I came with some bananas in a tanker.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.320
You mean the same way the redback 
spider came to Japan?!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.510
Redback spiders are incredibly poisonous.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.120
They came to Japan on ships,

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.320
and you can find them in parks.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.550
Everyone be careful!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.640
I see. So you entered illegally.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:17.490
We're about to go see the leaves in Kyoto.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.970
You wanna come too, Takkun?

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.900
No, I'm good.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.450
Come on. With all of us like 
this, we seem like a family.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.200
I'm the youngest one here!

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.370
Don't be so embarrassed.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.680
Autumn in Kyoto is great.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.200
Let's go on a date at the Kamo River.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.380
I can't just go on a trip 'cause I feel like it.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.550
Hmph! You never spend any time with me!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.590
Yetchi, let's go.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.210
Go? How?

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.470
You're going by sea?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.930
<b>Some time later...</b>

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.890
I'm back!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.180
Kyoto was fun!

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.860
I got you a Shinsengumi 
manjuu as a present.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.860
Shinsengumi Manjuu
 Serizawa Kamo

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.970
Welcome back.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.760
Serizawa?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:03.820
Why?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.370
Mine's Kondou Isami-cchi.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.200
Mine's Hijikata Toshizou!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.390
Hiichan got Okita Souji!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.500
Michael

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.960
What's Michael supposed to be from?!

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.310
So where's Yeti?

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.170
She already returned to the Himalayas.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.170
Here's a picture we took there.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.630
Foreigners are really interested 
in katana, aren't they?

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.090
Really?

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.060
From her face, it looks like 
you put her up to it...

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.840
<b>Truth</b>

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.940
<b>Shinsengumi</b>

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:47.660
Making one herself

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.660
Muromi-san.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.970
Once again, I have cut a worthless object.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.010
That's a harpy, isn't it?!

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.660
Yeah, a bird.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:39.870
A monster that appears in Greek 
mythology that's half man and half bird.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.330
Kind of a minor character, though.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.370
If you want to learn more, 
look it up on Wikipedia.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.670
Bye!

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.550
Harpy, Harpy.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.270
She says her name's Harpy.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:53.050
I found her stuck in a trap and saved her.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.150
Fine. Just don't get near me with her.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:57.730
Huh?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.610
Why?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.900
I want you to become good 
friends with her too.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.660
Even if you're the one asking, Yeti, 
there's some things I just can't do.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:11.500
You can't have peace between birds and fish!

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.160
<b>Rumble</b>

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.580
She's got the eyes of a predator right now!

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.060
<b>Eat Fish</b>

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.260
The eyes of a predator!

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.220
Harpy, no.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:34.200
Muromi-san's my f-friend.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.570
So she's not food.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.880
She's going to be friends with you, too.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.360
Harpy is Yeti's friend.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.250
Yeti is Muromi-san's friend.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.360
Friends of friends are friends!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.110
That's a dumb way of thinking!

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.280
Step

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.280
Step

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.320
Step

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.490
You bird-brain!

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.200
You're a bird, so you took three steps

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.210
and forgot what just happened, didn't you?!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:09.120
<b>We can't show what's happening, 
so enjoy these pictures instead.</b>

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:15.680
She really got me good.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.850
M-Muromi-san...

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:21.140
It's fine. I'm used to it.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.420
Harpy is Yeti's friend.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.470
Yeti is Muromi-san's friend.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.900
Friends of friends are friends!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.650
Don't chirp, you bird!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.730
Don't walk, you bird of prey!

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.320
You understand now, don't you Yetchi?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.540
You can't escape from the 
curse that is the food chain.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.020
<b>Blank</b>

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.370
Muromi-san.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.020
The weather's nice. Maybe I'll 
just go to sleep like this.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.170
Thanks for the lift.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.890
Where's Muromi-san?

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.410
Are Japan's air defenses failing now?

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.570
This is Harpy the harpy.

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:14.450
Harpy? You mean the ones 
from Greek mythology?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.990
Harpies have faces like old women, feathers of vultures, 
and talons of eagles. They have a strong appetite 
and a never-ending hunger, and are forced to move 
from each feast to the next. When they see food, 
they gobble it down in an unsightly manner, 
and leave behind their scattered waste and leftovers. 
They do not die, and release a foul odor 
and noise that is offensive to the ears...

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.600
It doesn't look like they're saying 
anything good about them.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.580
Who're you? Who're you?

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.730
Hey there.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.200
My name is Takurou.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.550
Takurou!

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:27.690
Step

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.230
Takurou!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:28.060
Step

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:28.520
Step

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:29.470
Taku—

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:29.730
Blank

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:31.420
Huh?

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:33.410
Who're you? Who're you?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.660
What?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.770
She can't remember any minor 
events after taking three steps.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.780
Who? Who?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:39.890
She's a bird!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.150
She's acting 100% on instinct!

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.580
She's a bird with the face of a person.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:48.060
Actually, I thought birds were 
Muromi-san's natural enemies.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:50.440
I just have to get it

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.360
deep into Harpy's subconscious 
that Muromi-san isn't food.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:59.030
Then they should be able 
to get along just fine.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.020
So she really did treat 
Muromi-san like food.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.920
Archerfish Style! Compressed Water Cannon!

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.170
Did you see the true strength of us fish?!

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:17.020
I don't think she intends to 
get along with her at all.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.840
She's out just like that?!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:25.570
You're mine if you come into the water!

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:28.230
The water is my territory!

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:29.970
Oh, she ran away.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.730
I wonder if she'll be 
able to shake her off.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.710
Oneetan, you can do it!

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:34.940
You guys were here?!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.150
It's a suicide attack by Harpy!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.290
She's going in the water.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.470
Muromi's gonna get caught.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.710
Let go of me!

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.340
And she let go of her.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.850
And now caught her again.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.530
Well, this just goes to show you can't

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:49.880
defy the laws of mother nature.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:50.770
Indeed.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.300
Oneetan...

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:02.720
Even if you defeat me, 
the other mermaids will...

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.100
That's not happening.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.520
What villain king are you supposed to be?

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.510
You seem like the bad guy in all of this.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:09.760
Yeah.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.690
Guess I'll have to do something.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.460
Harpy, come here.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.190
Dried Krill

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.270
Step

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:14.760
Step

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:15.060
{fad\(80,53)}Step

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.190
Reset

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.550
Here you go.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.920
Listen up, Harpy.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.820
That big fish over there 
isn't food or your enemy,

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.680
she's your friend, so you 
shouldn't attack her.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:26.660
Now, repeat.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.160
Muromi-san is Harpy's friend.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.980
She looks tasty, but she's my 
friend, so I can't attack her.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:32.760
Well done.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.240
I want more! More!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.990
Here you go.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:39.380
I guess that means when you train 
someone, you start with food.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.430
You stupid bird!

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.390
Remorse.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:51.910
Harpy loves fish.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:52.650
They're good, aren't they?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.520
I'm going to eat Muromi-san.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:54.010
No.

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:55.000
Fine. I'll bite her.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.130
That's the same thing.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:56.680
Taste her.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:57.440
I said no.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.170
Gulp her down.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.630
Hey, wait. Bite her?

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:05.830
Next Time: 
Muromi-san and Twin Mountain

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:04.390
Bite! Bite! Bite! Bite! Bite! Bite!

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:04.390
Harpy, you're a bird, but you have teeth?
